WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.610
When using automatic stitch patterning,

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.900
we don't want to distort the edges of our

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:13.140
knitting. By taking time to ensure
that the edge needles knit and not pattern

4
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:18.260
will make it easier to seam piece
and to work increases and decreases.

5
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:21.140
For example, when knitting tuck or slip,

6
00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.740
we don't want those edge
stitches to tuck or slip.

7
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.340
When knitting with a lace carriage,

8
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.780
we certainly don't want the edge
stitch to be an eyelet.

9
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.340
Preventing the edge stitches

10
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:37.700
from patterning is important and it's done
differently depending on your machine.

11
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.700
On this Singer machine,
with this stitch pattern,

12
00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:46.180
I can't easily predict when a tuck is
going to occur on the edge stitch.

13
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.580
Here I can see the tuck stitches on this

14
00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.520
row and the edge stitch is
knitting correctly.

15
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:03.800
But on this row the pattern is
trying to tuck the end needle.

16
00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:22.400
By tucking the edge stitch,
the knitting will be distorted.

17
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.180
To prevent this, put the end needle,

18
00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:34.900
maybe two needles into"D" position or
pull them all the way out every row.

19
00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:40.560
This will prevent those stitches
from tucking or patterning.

20
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.420
Now when I work a decrease,
I'll have two plain stitches and I'm not

21
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.480
messing around with tuck
strands on the edges.

22
00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.020
If you look closely,
the tucked edge will be more difficult

23
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:57.200
to seam where the plain edge will
be neater and easier to seam.

